# Build inputs and outputs. bun.lock is NOT here on purpose: the Nix build
# installs node_modules from it (nix/bun-deps.nix), so it has to be committed
# and has to stay in step with package.json.
#
# `dist/` being listed here is load-bearing, not tidiness. Tailwind v4 detects
# its own sources by walking the project and skipping whatever git ignores, so
# an unignored dist/ makes each build scan the PREVIOUS build's CSS and JS and
# re-emit every class it finds there. Measured: 24.3 kB of CSS became 37.5 kB,
# and it would have kept ratcheting. With dist/ ignored, two builds in a row
# produce byte-identical hashed filenames.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# LosOS Lab's core, generated by `bun run lab:core` (cargo + wasm-bindgen
# from admin-ui/lab/core); the build step writes it, git never carries it.
src/lab/core-pkg/
# The Lab's WebAssembly libvirt client, generated by `bun run lab:virt`
# (admin-ui/lab/virt-rpc); imported only when a guest starts on that path.
src/lab/virt-pkg/
# The Lab's GPU canvas (admin-ui/lab/render), both backends, generated by
# `bun run lab:render`; loaded only when the page swaps its SVG canvas out.
src/lab/render-pkg/
# losos-mdx (backend/mdx) for the browser, generated by `bun run mdx`:
# LosOS Office's editor and Notes parse and draw documents with it.
src/mdx/pkg/
# Classes the no-JavaScript pages use. Generated from the Rust sources into
# a Turso database and the text `@source` scans (scripts/basic-classes.mjs).
# Gitignored on purpose: a committed copy is a merge conflict, and Tailwind
# skips gitignored files unless a sheet names them with `@source`.
src/styles/basic-classes.txt
src/styles/basic-classes.db
